          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The First 30 Minutes After Waking Are Not Like The Rest Of The Day",
            "text": "The transition into wakefulness appears to shape how the rest of the day begins.",
            "research_insight": "The first thirty minutes after waking appear to represent a distinct transitional period rather than an ordinary extension of the day. Our review of emerging research suggests this window may respond differently to sensory input than later waking hours.",
